section__
  @title "T169 - ACT3 - The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/03-act3-crownlands/frame-169.jpg"

  "Mud and horse dung stew in the gate trench while smoke from pitch baskets stings your eyes. Riverlands refugees sleep under torn sailcloth against the city wall, and ravens from Castle Black still carry yesterday's warning: the Watch can hold the Wall, but not another month without grain. Cersei Lannister watches from the parapet with a bored smile, Joffrey Baratheon watches with naked hunger, and the street priests count how many hungry mouths stand between your oath and rebellion.

Act Three begins as a problem of enforcement, not persuasion. Bread carts vanish before sunrise, Gold Cloaks sell exemptions by alley, and every lord who called himself neutral in Act Two now demands coin or hostages to keep his men inside the city line. If you rule in daylight, rivals can predict you. If you rule from shadows, allies start measuring the price of betrayal. Either way, the capital must be made governable before nightfall.

The account in front of you is brutal: honor=${honor}, ruthlessness=${ruthlessness}, secrecy=${secrecy}, leverage=${leverage}, war_readiness=${war_readiness}, wealth=${wealth}, north_trust=${north_trust}, crown_trust=${crown_trust}, watch_trust=${watch_trust}, essos_ties=${essos_ties}, dragon_factor=${dragon_factor}, survival_clock=${survival_clock}. History has already opened its ledger; this choice decides what gets written first."

  choice__
    @target "T170 - ACT3 - Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action crown_trust = clampStat(crown_trust + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Read riot terms from the gatehouse steps, bind the Gold Cloaks to written law, and carry the blame in daylight."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T171 - ACT3 - Qarth Alliance Split near the godswood"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Pay butcher-guild informers to stage a convenient confession, then cash the panic into leverage over wavering houses."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "T170 - ACT3 - Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/03-act3-crownlands/frame-170.jpg"

  "Salt spray drifts off Blackwater Bay, mixing with fish blood and lamp oil along the chain tower. Harbor crews whisper that northern wagons were stripped before reaching Flea Bottom, and men who swore to your muster in Act Two now melt into alleys before dusk. Bronn leans on the quay rail like violence is a coin he can spend at will, while Varys tracks every dockmaster's glance for signs of revolt.

City stability hangs on who controls arrivals: grain, rumor, and armed men. If captains believe decrees are theater, they will sell berth rights to whoever pays fastest and starve your districts by accident or design. If you crack down too hard, merchants will close their holds and call it weather delay while the crowd grows feral. The harbor is the kingdom's throat; today you either clear it or let someone else place a hand there.

Your position compresses to numbers and hours: honor=${honor}, ruthlessness=${ruthlessness}, secrecy=${secrecy}, leverage=${leverage}, war_readiness=${war_readiness}, wealth=${wealth}, north_trust=${north_trust}, crown_trust=${crown_trust}, watch_trust=${watch_trust}, essos_ties=${essos_ties}, dragon_factor=${dragon_factor}, survival_clock=${survival_clock}. One decision now decides whether order arrives by law, fear, or foreign debt."

  choice__
