section__
  @title "T171 - ACT3 - Qarth Alliance Split near the godswood"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/03-act3-crownlands/frame-171.jpg"

  "Wax gutters down the wall sconces in the godswood court while rain taps the elm leaves overhead. Creditors from Qarth and Gulltown crowd the benches with armed scribes, each claiming repayment priority for loans that kept your Act Two campaign moving. Varys presents ledgers with polite poison in every line, and Bronn keeps a hand near his dagger in case negotiation turns into collection.

This is where blackmail economics meets crowd politics. If debt houses believe the city treasury is soft, they will fund rival claimants before midnight and call it prudent diversification. If you humiliate them publicly, they can freeze grain insurance, and your food riots become your fault by morning. The realm will read this hearing as proof that either law still exists in King's Landing or only private coercion does.

You measure margin against collapse: honor=${honor}, ruthlessness=${ruthlessness}, secrecy=${secrecy}, leverage=${leverage}, war_readiness=${war_readiness}, wealth=${wealth}, north_trust=${north_trust}, crown_trust=${crown_trust}, watch_trust=${watch_trust}, essos_ties=${essos_ties}, dragon_factor=${dragon_factor}, survival_clock=${survival_clock}. The wrong creditor leaves this chamber richer and the city poorer."

