section__
  @title "T172 - ACT3 - The Wall War Map against old law"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/03-act3-crownlands/frame-172.jpg"

  "Copper dust hangs in the mint quarter and turns your tongue bitter while boys sprint raven tubes between counting houses. Joffrey wants punishments announced before supper, Cersei wants deniability if they fail, and dock guild envoys wait outside with seals ready for whichever story survives the hour. Three different copies of your last decree are already circulating, and only one carries your actual wording.

Regime control now depends on information discipline. If your enemies can edit orders faster than you can enforce them, every patrol commander becomes a local king and every crowd judges law by rumor. A clean public record may cost you flexibility, but covert manipulation may poison trust in your own chain of command. This decision determines whether the Crownlands obey one center or fracture into profitable confusion.

The numbers refuse sentiment: honor=${honor}, ruthlessness=${ruthlessness}, secrecy=${secrecy}, leverage=${leverage}, war_readiness=${war_readiness}, wealth=${wealth}, north_trust=${north_trust}, crown_trust=${crown_trust}, watch_trust=${watch_trust}, essos_ties=${essos_ties}, dragon_factor=${dragon_factor}, survival_clock=${survival_clock}. You are not choosing comfort, only which cost reaches you first."

