  "Braziers spit iron sparks along guild row where quartermasters haggle like slavers over sacks of flour. Court agents report northern caravans delayed by mud and raids, echoing the promises you made when the Wall pleaded for grain in Act Two. Cersei demands visible strength, Joffrey demands someone to blame, and every guildmaster waits to see whether your signatures still mean equal rationing or purchased favor.

This node is about legitimacy through logistics. If rations follow oath and need, you keep hard allies but surrender political leverage at court. If rations follow intimidation, the city quiets quickly while resentment hardens into future revolt. Either course will define who believes your banners protect them and who begins storing knives for when your patrols tire.

You calculate authority in shrinking margins: honor=${honor}, ruthlessness=${ruthlessness}, secrecy=${secrecy}, leverage=${leverage}, war_readiness=${war_readiness}, wealth=${wealth}, north_trust=${north_trust}, crown_trust=${crown_trust}, watch_trust=${watch_trust}, essos_ties=${essos_ties}, dragon_factor=${dragon_factor}, survival_clock=${survival_clock}. A ration mark on parchment now can decide a siege outcome months from now."

