  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/03-act3-crownlands/frame-174.jpg"

  "At Moat Cailin gatehouse, wet cloaks steam in torchlight while petitioners pound the outer doors for protection. Word of a failed levy sweep has spread through three districts, and now rival banner captains demand proof that the regime can police its own streets. Bronn offers names for immediate arrests, Varys offers cleaner outcomes with dirtier methods, and septons chant over the noise to claim moral custody of the crowd.

Crowd control politics punishes hesitation. A transparent crackdown can restore predictable order but exposes every mistake to witnesses and rival scribes. A covert removal campaign can quiet the streets by dawn while feeding whispers that you govern through kidnappers. Either approach buys control from one constituency and spends it with another, and sunrise will reveal which account you overdrew.

Your mandate balances on diminishing reserves: honor=${honor}, ruthlessness=${ruthlessness}, secrecy=${secrecy}, leverage=${leverage}, war_readiness=${war_readiness}, wealth=${wealth}, north_trust=${north_trust}, crown_trust=${crown_trust}, watch_trust=${watch_trust}, essos_ties=${essos_ties}, dragon_factor=${dragon_factor}, survival_clock=${survival_clock}. Enforcement is coming either way; the question is whose name the city curses."

