  "Tar smoke and brine roll through dockside as neutral house envoys arrive under white ribbons and concealed mail. They watched you survive Act Two and now demand payment for not choosing your enemies. Varys tracks who speaks first, Bronn tracks who brought enough men to betray the meeting, and Gold Cloaks form a thin line between negotiation and riot.

Neutrality in the Crownlands is now a commodity. If you lock these houses into public quota and patrol obligations, you gain predictable support but spend reputation and coin. If you buy betrayal in private, you can break one rival chain quickly while teaching every ally that loyalty is temporary and priced in secrets. A third path exists through foreign credit, but that debt arrives with foreign expectations and little mercy.

Your strategic balance sheet narrows by the hour: honor=${honor}, ruthlessness=${ruthlessness}, secrecy=${secrecy}, leverage=${leverage}, war_readiness=${war_readiness}, wealth=${wealth}, north_trust=${north_trust}, crown_trust=${crown_trust}, watch_trust=${watch_trust}, essos_ties=${essos_ties}, dragon_factor=${dragon_factor}, survival_clock=${survival_clock}. You can purchase calm tonight, but never without interest."

