  "Wax smoke curls along the city wall walk where missing helmets hang from pegs like accusations. Muster captains report deserters from three patrol districts, not because battle scares them, but because contradictory orders made them easy scapegoats. Joffrey demands immediate executions to set an example; Cersei wants recoverable assets, not martyrs. Moneylenders hover nearby, pricing what your command discipline is worth.

Regime enforcement fails fastest when officers believe policy changes with every whisper. A transparent reckoning can restore confidence in your chain of command, though it exposes royal weakness in public. A covert pardon network can refill ranks quickly, but it blurs loyalty into contract violence and hands tomorrow's blackmail to today's survivors. What you choose here sets the operating code for every future crackdown.

All choices cash out against the same reserve: honor=${honor}, ruthlessness=${ruthlessness}, secrecy=${secrecy}, leverage=${leverage}, war_readiness=${war_readiness}, wealth=${wealth}, north_trust=${north_trust}, crown_trust=${crown_trust}, watch_trust=${watch_trust}, essos_ties=${essos_ties}, dragon_factor=${dragon_factor}, survival_clock=${survival_clock}. The city will obey someone by dawn; decide whether it is your law or your fear."

