  "Highgarden Siege Promise in the throne shadow throws you into streets where every decree is tested before the ink dries. Rainwater and ash run through the gutters, and boiled barley stings the air from relief kettles near the gates. Varys counts who listens, Bronn counts who can be broken, and dock guild factors wait to see whether your word still carries penalties. After the Watch warnings and northern concessions from Act Two, the Crownlands now demand proof that sacrifice bought actual control.

If you over-correct with force, you risk coordinated backlash; if you delay for consensus, you surrender initiative to houses already preparing private militias. This is regime enforcement in its ugliest form: if you choose transparent process, you spend time and prestige; if you choose hidden pressure, you gain speed while corroding trust in the same chain of command you need tomorrow.

You can feel the margin narrowing in hard values: honor=${honor}, ruthlessness=${ruthlessness}, secrecy=${secrecy}, leverage=${leverage}, war_readiness=${war_readiness}, wealth=${wealth}, north_trust=${north_trust}, crown_trust=${crown_trust}, watch_trust=${watch_trust}, essos_ties=${essos_ties}, dragon_factor=${dragon_factor}, survival_clock=${survival_clock}. By dawn, the city will remember whichever method you chose, not the reason you chose it."

