  "Riverrun Broken Oath under rain throws you into a capital already cracking under ration lines and patrol fatigue. Sea wind carries brine, tar, and rot from Blackwater Bay while torch smoke hangs low over the alleys. Court clerks bring conflicting writs, septons demand visible justice, and street captains ask who will absorb the blood cost of compliance. Decisions that held the realm together in Act Two have arrived as unpaid invoices, and each faction expects to be paid first.

This is regime enforcement in its ugliest form: if you choose transparent process, you spend time and prestige; if you choose hidden pressure, you gain speed while corroding trust in the same chain of command you need tomorrow. Crowd control politics leaves no neutral ground; public discipline stabilizes legitimacy but invites open challenge, while covert coercion quiets districts and teaches everyone that fear is the only currency.

